        "original_id": "6f93e052-32bc-5c8a-bb93-372ab877f842",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Aleksei Gan, Nicholas II\n- Places: Russian Empire, Russia\n- Roles: anarchist, avant-garde artist, art theorist, graphic designer, emperor\n- Events: Russian Revolution, February Revolution of 1917\n- Organizations: provisional government\n\nFacts:\n- Aleksei Gan was born in 1887 or 1893 and died in 1942.\n- Aleksei Gan was a Russian anarchist, avant-garde artist, art theorist, and graphic designer.\n- During the February Revolution of 1917, the Russian Empire collapsed after Emperor Nicholas II abdicated.\n- During the first revolution of February 1917, the old regime in Russia was replaced by a provisional government.\n- Russia was using the Julian calendar at the time, so February 1917 in Russia corresponded to March 1917 in the Gregorian calendar.",
